.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt SYNC 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sync
.Nd write cached data to the disks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes everything the system holds in memory for its disks out to them, with
.Xr sync 2 .
It is rarely needed: the file system writes through, and
.Xr reboot 8
synchronizes before restarting.
Arguments are ignored.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sync 2 ,
.Xr reboot 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v4 .
